{
  "_": [
    "The paint plan for the Russian font atlases: which Cyrillic letter goes",
    "into which glyph cell of the retail font, and where its shape comes from.",
    "Cells are the retail glyph table's (pkztool font Main.pak <font>); the",
    "slot for a letter is its Windows-1251 code, which lands on an accented",
    "Latin letter's cell (the runtime folds Cyrillic to those codes, and the",
    "letters that look like Latin ones -- А В Е К М Н О Р С Т Х, а е о р с у х --",
    "to the Latin letters, so those need no cell). A source is a box in the",
    "Shattered Dimensions PC atlas (res/textures/SDPC_*), which has the same",
    "typefaces with Cyrillic drawn, or the retail atlas's own glyph, sometimes",
    "with the crossbar erased (Л from A). ref is the retail glyph whose height",
    "the pasted shape is scaled to. Only the letters of the test text and their",
    "capitals are painted so far; the rest of the alphabet still shows the",
    "accented Latin letter its slot holds."
  ],
